  "idea": "Typeform vs Tally: comparing the sleek form builder with the free challenger",
  "text": "Here is the direct comparison between Typeform's famous interface and Tally's Notion-style simplicity. Building multi-step intake quizzes inside Typeform feels clunky, slow, and restricted by rigid design panels. The rigid single-question layout often frustrates desktop users, causing steep drop-offs on long surveys. Tally lets you type forms like Notion docs with instant conditional logic and native webhooks. You launch clean client intake flows in minutes.",
